Size evaluate()'s per-class statistics by the model's class count (correctness: genuine execution bug).

Demonstrated failure (run training-preflight, WLASL2000, --num_classes 2000):
  File "/opt/spoter/spoter/utils.py", line 52, in evaluate
    stats[int(labels[0][0])][1] += 1
  KeyError: 1158
evaluate() hardcodes `stats = {i: [0, 0] for i in range(101)}`, so any label >= 101 crashes validation and
test. SPOTER itself was only run with 100 classes. The dict only feeds the optional per-label printout;
accuracy computation is unchanged.

diff --git a/spoter/utils.py b/spoter/utils.py
index af40226..e67b799 100644
--- a/spoter/utils.py
+++ b/spoter/utils.py
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ def train_epoch(model, dataloader, criterion, optimizer, device, scheduler=None)
 def evaluate(model, dataloader, device, print_stats=False):
 
     pred_correct, pred_all = 0, 0
-    stats = {i: [0, 0] for i in range(101)}
+    stats = {i: [0, 0] for i in range(model.linear_class.out_features)}
 
     for i, data in enumerate(dataloader):
         inputs, labels = data
